      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6594357456bbb024d369b0ba|full_name} Indeed! Currently all VRC Object Sync scripts require continuous syncing, which is not only a network strain, but adds a boatload of unnecessary calls and, ludicrously, slows down the frame. We've had very good results with Smart Object Sync in testing and I'm currently using it in all worlds. Once Lightsync becomes production-ready, I'll happily apply that system in all worlds, which apparently is even 2x faster than the current implementation, which is already dozens, if not hundreds of times faster than VRC's own object sync.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
